I wrote the review to `C:\tenderloin-redux\kibitz-runs\2026-10-18-first-playable\r3\claude.md`. The file-access check passed, and I made no other file changes.

**Verdict: yes-with-fixes.** The game logic, save handling and routing fit together, and the local server doesn't let requests reach files outside `public/`. Three things need fixing before build:

1. **A crash in "Start fresh" (`game.js:155`).** If the street data hasn't loaded, or failed to load, Settings → "Start a new afternoon…" → "Start fresh" throws an error. The dialog stays open and the reset is never saved. The fix is a one-line guard: `if (world) world.path = [];`.
2. **The browser test isn't connected to the server it checks (`tests/browser-smoke.mjs`).**
   - It always uses port 4173, even though the server reads `PORT`.
   - It doesn't start the server itself, so an old server left running on 4173 could give a false pass.
   - It requires an installed Google Chrome.
   - It records "keyboard: pass" after a single arrow-key press, so BUILD_STATUS would claim keyboard coverage that was never tested.
3. **Keyboard focus is lost after every placement in both grid editors (`game.js:79`, `game.js:96`).** The grid cells have no `id`, so `show()` can't put focus back after redrawing the dialog. Keyboard users have to Tab back to their spot after each placement. Adding ids to the cells fixes it.

The review also has nine should-fix items, with file:line evidence for each:
- The animation loop stops for good if one frame throws an error.
- The music button keeps focus, so WASD and the arrow keys stop working until you click the map.
- Tap targets on narrow screens are very small, and there's no tap equivalent of the E key. The roadmap puts touch play in M1, so this isn't an M0 blocker.
- A corrupt settings value makes the game say saving is unavailable even when it works.
- Music can end up playing while the button shows it as off.
- Placement messages may not be read out by screen readers.
- After a reload, the editors select a supply or motif that's already placed instead of the next missing one.
- The server can crash if a file read fails after the response has started.
- Leaving the tab doesn't save the player's position.

It lists three bits of unused code that can be cut: the `'move'` action, `dispose()` and `.text-link`.

Some connected services (Asana, Atlassian, Datadog, GitHub, Linear, Notion, PagerDuty, Slack, Box, Runway) need authorizing before they can be used. Claude.ai connectors are authorized in your claude.ai connector settings; the others through `claude mcp` or `/mcp` in an interactive session. This review didn't need any of them.
